From 87b5eed3222f9288e7edec01a140862342040b43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 22:37:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wifipro: lock the 2.4 GHz Preamble select while 802.11b is
 disabled (owner request 2026-08-05)

The Disable-802.11b row (rateset) is now the master of the Preamble row
(plcphdr): selecting Disable forces the Preamble select to its
Disable-802.11b state (plcphdr "0" - the value the stock page derives
rateset from) and locks it (dimmed, not editable); switching back to
Allow unlocks it and restores the pre-lock selection (a queued preamble
change is parked while locked, not lost). The "0" option is no longer
user-pickable - it exists only as the locked display state. A locked
plcphdr is staged only together with a staged rateset=ofdm, so a
pre-existing inconsistent nvram pair (rateset=ofdm with plcphdr=long,
producible by the previously-independent controls) no longer surfaces
as a phantom pending change at page load. Page-side only; no backend
change. Mock-validated (render + locked-at-load + zero-staged).
